CHAPTER.VERS:
And Yahweh said to Moses, Yet one plague more I will bring on Pharaoh, and on Egypt; afterward he will let you

          {+}
         go from here: when he will let you

          {+}
         go, he will surely thrust you

          {+}
         out from here altogether.

But against any of the sons of Israel will not a dog move his tongue, against man or beast: that you

          {+}
         may know how that Yahweh does make a distinction between the Egyptians and Israel.

And Yahweh said to Moses, Pharaoh will not listen to you

          {+}
        ; that my wonders may be multiplied in the land of Egypt.
